S.W.SQUIRES [scott]          at 02:56 EDT
 
  Thanks for all the feedback Alan.  Sounds like you're quite involved with
these areas.
   I have looked at some of the optical and laser techniques when I was at the
SPIE show this year.  Would rather keep it a bit simpler.
   Your thoughts on tape are good.  We were looking at a bit lower tech. The
tape would have two or more parallel patterns each being read with a separate
simple photodetector.  This would allow some fault tolerance.  The tape would
probably be out of plastic and mounted to channel on the track to avoid being
stepped on.  Mounting the tape on the side or upside down might also be done. 
Relative marks would probably be fine but if not we might use something
similar to the SMPTE code.  A single 'channel' of data should suffice if done
correctly.      -scott

