Category 6,  Topic 9
Message 14        Sun Oct 02, 1988
S.W.SQUIRES [scott]          at 03:36 EDT
 
Those interested in Robotics and AI may want to check the October issue of 
OMNI magazine.  There is a article on the insect robots designed by Rodney 
Brooks at MIT's Artificial Intelligence Laboratory.  The potential 
applications and approaches are discussed.  The article includes step by  step
instructions on how to modify a cheap toy car from Radio Shack and add 
electonics to simulate some of the responses of an insect.  ($50-75 total) 
All the logic is actually photocells, Op Amps and TTL logic but a person 
should be able to replace that logic with a small Forth board that does  that
and much more.  As I recall Scientific American had a Computer Recreations
article a couple of years ago describing similar photocell controlled
vehicles.   -scott
